            <ArticleTitle>Relationship between HLA haplotype and BMI change in Japanese slowly progressive type 1 diabetes patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0168-8227(16)31777-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2016.12.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We investigated the association between susceptible HLA and BMI change rate from diagnosis of diabetes to diagnosis of slowly progressive type 1 diabetes in Japanese diabetic patients. Subjects with the HLA DRB1*04:05-DQB1*04:01 haplotype were more likely to show weight loss than those without. This HLA haplotype might affect weight loss.</AbstractText>
